# ============================================================================
#  frontend-app/.env - build-time variables for the PWA (Vite)
# ============================================================================
#  Only VITE_* values are inlined into the bundle; everything else must not
#  go here (secrets would end up in the browser). The real .env is gitignored.
#  The API base defaults to "/api" (same origin) - this file is therefore
#  optional. Create it only to override:
#    cp .env.example .env
#  Values are baked in at build time, so re-run `npm run build` after changing
#  them (the API reads its own backend/.env at runtime, not this file).
# ============================================================================
#  "/api" keeps the app same-origin: the NestJS backend serves both the API
#  (/api/*) and this PWA build, and on a VPS Nginx proxies /api to the backend
#  on 127.0.0.1:3000. Never point this at localhost from a phone - localhost
#  there is the phone itself.
#  Use a full URL (https://api.example.com/api) only when the API lives on
#  another origin; that origin must then allow CORS (the backend does).
VITE_API_URL="/api"
